From: Your Name <godkiller_nt@hammermaps.de>
Date: Tue, 8 Sep 2026 01:43:08 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Implement Phase A of the Hybrid AI Core framework scaffold

Per docs/designs/hybrid-ai-core-phase-a.md (Approach B: engine-free
core / engine-aware adapter split):

- dlls/ai_hybrid_core.h/.cpp: no HLSDK includes. AITacticalAction enum,
  AIHybridCapabilityFlags, AIProfile, ClampScore/Clamp01/DecayConfidence,
  ActionName/ActionSupported, and the dormant AIHybridState + its
  Phase-A no-op UpdateSnapshot(). Compiles and tests standalone.
- dlls/ai_hybrid.h/.cpp: the only file in this subsystem that includes
  engine headers. Reads the ai_hybrid/ai_hybrid_debug CVars and prints
  bounded debug output.
- dlls/game.h/.cpp: register ai_hybrid (default 0) and ai_hybrid_debug
  (default 0) alongside the existing CVAR block, same convention as
  every other server CVar.
- dlls/hgrunt.cpp: CHGrunt gets a dormant m_AIHybridState member,
  zero-initialized in Spawn() (entity-slot reuse safety), observed and
  logged from PrescheduleThink(). GetSchedule() is untouched - action
  stays AI_ACTION_NONE, zero behavior change while ai_hybrid is 0
  (verified: rebuilt client.so is byte-identical to the pre-change
  baseline, only hl.so differs).
- tests/ai_hybrid_core_tests.cpp + scripts/run-ai-hybrid-core-tests.sh:
  standalone host tests (no engine headers, no DLL link) covering
  ActionName/ActionSupported/Clamp01/ClampScore/DecayConfidence/
  UpdateSnapshot. Wired into `make check` in linux/Makefile (Linux
  only for Phase A, per the design doc's Windows follow-up note).

